SELECT PARTITION_NAME, PARTITION_DESCRIPTION
FROM INFORMATION_SCHEMA.PARTITIONS
WHERE TABLE_SCHEMA = 'product_db'
AND TABLE_NAME = 'product';
Partitioning divides a large table into smaller parts called partitions based on a particular column. In this practical, we partitioned the PRODUCT table using Range Partitioning based on product price. Products below ₹1,000 are stored in p_low, products between ₹1,000 and ₹5,000 are stored in p_mid, and expensive products are stored in p_high. MySQL automatically stores, moves and deletes records from the appropriate partitions during DML operations. Partition-wise retrieval improves performance by accessing only the required partition, reducing unnecessary data scanning.

